.TH NYSM-TRAY 1 "" "Now You See Me" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nysm-tray \- live system values in the top bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nysm-tray
[\fB\-\-attach\fR \fIauto\fR|\fInever\fR|\fIrequire\fR]
[\fB\-\-items\fR \fIlist\fR]
[\fB\-\-meter\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-label\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nysm-tray
shows CPU usage, memory in use, network download and upload, storage used
on
.I /
and disk activity in the desktop's top bar, through the
StatusNotifier/AppIndicator protocol (built into Ubuntu; KDE, XFCE and
others). Text next to the icons needs Ubuntu's AppIndicator host; other
desktops show the icons.
.PP
Its menu opens the desktop app
.RB ( nysm-desktop ),
chooses what the top bar shows (items, icons, names, compact strip) and
quits. Choices are saved in the configuration file. A warning sign appears
while an alert fires.
.PP
The tray reads from the shared collector
.RB ( "nysm service run" )
when one runs, and collects on its own otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-attach " " \fIauto\fR|\fInever\fR|\fIrequire\fR
Use the shared collector when available (default), never, or only.
.TP
.BI \-\-items " list"
Comma-separated items: cpu, mem, net, storage, disk, diskio.
.TP
.B \-\-meter
One compact two-bar icon instead of values.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-label
Icons only, no text.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nysm/config.toml
Settings, including the top-bar items
.RB ( "nysm config show" ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/nysm-tray.desktop
Present when "Start at login" is on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nysm (1),
.BR nysm-desktop (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sheheemmulakkal/now-you-see-me
